<title>USA: Johnson Controls files for $1.5 bln shelf.</title>
<headline>Johnson Controls files for $1.5 bln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Johnson Controls Inc said Friday it filed a universal shelf registration for $1.5 billion with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>It said the registration covers issuance of a variety of debt and equity instruments.</p>
<p>On Monday, Johnson Controls, an automotive seating manufacturer, completed the $1.35 billion acquisition of privately held Prince Automotive.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
